 This changelog tracks the current release line. Historical phase notes
 and stale roadmap entries have been removed from the public documentation set.
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+- `j2k-jpeg` coefficient extraction can retain quantized blocks without a
+  duplicate dequantized plane. MCU-window extraction keeps only requested
+  baseline blocks, uses restart intervals when present, and exposes a
+  header-only working-set estimate. The new lossless crop API re-emits
+  baseline or progressive Huffman sources as MCU-aligned baseline crops while
+  preserving JFIF/Adobe colour signalling, SOF component identifiers, and
+  independent component quantization tables. Progressive and multi-scan
+  crops still require whole-image coefficient accumulation.
+
 ## [0.13.1] - 2026-10-29
 
 - `CpuBatchDecoder` region and region-plus-reduced requests no longer
